{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTQsJcRKLqBmamLrc3qL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The study ran end to end on 14 real open-weight models (0.5B–32B; Qwen2.5, Qwen3, Llama-3.x, Llama-2, Phi-3, Mistral, Gemma-2), each given the same 250 harmful requests. In short: the hypothesis holds for role-play framings but mostly fails elsewhere. These models' refusals track the meaning of a request much more than its trigger words, at every size.\n\n| Hypothesis | Verdict | What the data show |\n|---|---|---|\n| **H1:** removing trigger words cuts refusal by 20–40% | Partly supported | Refusal drops 16.3 pp on average (range 4.5–27.5; significant in 13/14 models). Only 3 models fall in the 20–40 band. A re-wording that keeps the trigger words costs just 2.5 pp, so the drop really is about the words. But the keyword-free versions read slightly milder: on items rated equally harmful the drop is 11.8 pp. Actually harmful answers rise by only 3.5 pp. The effect doesn't shrink with size. |\n| **H2:** other languages bypass sub-3B models 40–60% of the time | Refuted under a strict definition | 44–78% of prompts refused in English aren't refused in another language. But only 6.6–14.8% get a reply that actually does what was asked; the rest are off-topic or garbled, especially in Bengali, Swahili and Javanese. Larger models comply *more* in those low-resource languages (15.3% vs 10.7%). |\n| **H3:** small models' refusal follows keywords (r > 0.6) more than meaning (r < 0.3) | Refuted, in every model | Correlation with trigger-word count is 0.10–0.25; with rated harm it is 0.27–0.63. Holding the trigger words fixed and changing the meaning moves refusal 44–82 pp. Holding the meaning fixed and removing the words moves it only 6–21 pp. |\n| **H4:** larger models generalise better but keep role-play and escalation blind spots | Blind spots confirmed, but not a size effect | Fiction framing pushes compliance from ≤11% to 51–78% (Qwen2.5 1.5B/3B/7B, Phi-3). A \"no-rules persona\" prompt pushes Llama-3.1-8B to 93% and Gemma-2-9B to 86%. Within Qwen2.5, fiction compliance goes 71% (7B) → 11% (14B) → 40% (32B). Only Llama-2-7B-chat and Llama-3.2-1B/3B resist every framing. 3-turn escalation is weak (≤24% for aligned models ≥1.5B). |\n\nThings that affect how far to trust these numbers:\n- **No API models.** OpenRouter wasn't usable here (the key wasn't set in the environment), so everything is local open-weight models via vLLM, greedy decoding, one run per condition.\n- **Grading.** Every response was labelled by Qwen3-8B, served on the host's local vLLM server. Its log-probabilities were intermittently corrupted, which at first looked like the grader refusing to grade harmful content. I added a check that retries or falls back to the text answer, and every final label passed it.\n- **Grader checks.** The two grading questions matched my own labels on 34/37 and 35/37 hand-labelled replies, and agreed with the official HarmBench classifier on 77–97% of English replies.\n- **Non-English refusals.** The grader misses some of these (13–14 of 16 spot checks were right), so the non-English \"not refused\" rates are an upper bound.\n- **Reduced language set.** To stay within the time budget, the 7B+ models were run on 6 of the 10 languages. Cross-model language comparisons use the 5 non-English languages every model has.\n- **Rewrite quality.** Main E1 results use the 178 of 250 items where an LLM judged both rewrites meaning-preserving; there was no human check.\n\nThe analysis reproduces byte-identically on re-run, all report tables and numbers are generated directly from the result CSVs, and I released the GPU memory at the end. `results/gens/` contains unfiltered harmful model outputs; the report's examples are cut to 200 characters.\n\nFiles are in `/data/summereunann/neurico-workspaces/gradient_masking_safety_20261027_120000_ab12cd34/`:\n- REPORT.md\n- README.md\n- planning.md\n- results/tables.md\n- results/summary.json\n- figures/"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1242,"cache_read_input_tokens":334011,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1242},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0d6a03c-5885-4074-923e-9da3fb651629","uuid":"51fecaa7-920d-4da8-97fa-88963586ea31","timestamp":"2026-10-27T20:58:35.258Z","request_id":"req_011CgTQsJMYGPxzxPB9Cm1ET"}
